kettle — third-party attributions

This product depends on and/or adapts ideas from the following projects:

* Alacritty (alacritty_terminal, vte) — Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/alacritty/alacritty
  kettle uses alacritty_terminal for its VT parser, grid and scrollback model.

* WezTerm (portable-pty) — MIT
  https://github.com/wez/wezterm
  kettle uses portable-pty for cross-platform PTY / Windows ConPTY support, and
  its image-protocol implementations were used as a reference.

* cosmic-text / glyphon — MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Text shaping, font fallback and GPU glyph atlas.

* Contour — Apache-2.0
  Reference for the Sixel parser state machine.

* kitty — GPL-3.0 (specification consulted, no GPL code copied)
  https://github.com/kovidgoyal/kitty
  kettle-vt's kitty graphics protocol implementation
  (`kettle-vt/src/kitty.rs`, `placeholder.rs`) follows kitty's
  published spec: the image transfer / placement / animation /
  Unicode-placeholder model, chunk-reassembly semantics, and
  relative-placement chain are all kitty's design. The
  implementation is original code in Rust; we cite the
  specification author for the design.

* Terminator — GPL-3.0 (UX convention consulted, no GPL code copied)
  https://github.com/gnome-terminator/terminator
  kettle's tabs / splits / broadcast-input UX + default keybinds
  (`terminatorlib/config.py`, `terminatorlib/terminator.py`) are
  Terminator's convention: `Ctrl+Shift+O` for top/bottom split,
  `Ctrl+Shift+E` for left/right split, the `broadcast_all`
  group-input semantics scoped per-tab. The implementation is
  original Rust code; we cite the upstream as the convention's
  origin.

* Ghostty — MIT
  https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty
  kettle's `key = value` config syntax, the `theme` key behavior,
  and the `unfocused-split-opacity` default 0.7 all follow
  Ghostty's convention. The implementation is original; the
  surface (key names, parsing rules, defaults) matches
  Ghostty's so a user's Ghostty config drops in unchanged.

